{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.4,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "short_to_supply",
      "components": ["J7", "J8"],
      "pins": ["J7.1", "J7.2", "J8.1", "J8.2"],
      "nets": ["+12V"],
      "observed": "On the Power sheet the +12V rail wire is drawn running vertically through J7 pin 1 and J7 pin 2 with junctions at both pins (and the +12V symbol also feeds J8 pin 2), so pins 1 and 2 of the fan headers are on the +12V net rather than only pin 2.",
      "expected": "The specification lists only pin 2 of each fan header on the 12 V rail: 'the two fan-header 12 V pins (J7/J8 pin 2)'. On a standard 4-pin fan header pin 1 is the fan ground return, so it should be tied to GND, not to +12V.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Also on this net: ... and the two fan-header 12 V pins (`J7`/`J8` pin 2)."},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Power sheet: +12V power symbol wired down through J7 pin 1 and pin 2 (junction dots) and to the J8 connector"}
      ],
      "impact": "The fan's ground-return pin is held at +12 V, so a standard fan receives no return path (effectively reverse supply) and will not spin; the firmware's fan-stall monitor would then trip RunFailureReason and abort the oven run.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["J5", "U6"],
      "pins": ["J5.2", "U6.1", "U6.2"],
      "nets": ["HEATER"],
      "observed": "An additional 2-pin screw terminal J5 is drawn with pin 2 tied to the HEATER net (the ESP32 GPIO1 / U6 IN & DIAG_EN logic net) and pin 1 to GND.",
      "expected": "The specification describes exactly one heater output connector, J6, fed by the switched output of U6 (OUT pin 7). A connector placed directly on the 3.3 V GPIO1/HEATER control net is not described and would expose the MCU logic drive rather than the switched 12 V heater output.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "`OUT` (pin 7) feeds the heater connector `J6` pin 2"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "MCU sheet: Screw_Terminal_01x02 J5 pin 2 wired to the net labelled HEATER, pin 1 to GND"}
      ],
      "impact": "Any load attached to J5 is driven from the ESP32 GPIO1 logic net instead of the switched 12 V heater output, so it would not receive heater power and would load the GPIO.",
      "confidence": 0.3
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic matches the specification on all explicitly stated values and connections (SPI, CS, heater switch, power mux, buck, thermocouple channels, CC resistors, ILIM/SS/boot components), but the fan-header wiring appears to put +12V on pin 1 as well as pin 2 (spec and standard fan pinout require pin 1 = GND), and an unexplained extra screw terminal J5 sits on the GPIO1 HEATER control net."
}

